# Converter output -- generated from the user's own game install, never committed.
# The .gdignore marker itself IS tracked (see the negation below) so Godot never scans or
# imports this folder's contents as project resources, even right after a fresh convert run.
/build/*
!/build/.gdignore

# Content packs are generated from the user's own game install and embed real extracted
# pixel/audio data -- never committed, same rule as /build/. The registry is the one thing
# under /packs/ that's original-authored (an ID -> semantic-name mapping, no game bytes) and
# safe to track, so it's carved out below the same way build/.gdignore is. packs/.gdignore
# is tracked too (see the engine's game/pack.gd) so Godot's editor never scans/imports pack PNGs
# as project resources -- packs are loaded at runtime via FileAccess/Image, never res://.
/packs/*
!/packs/registry/
!/packs/.gdignore

# Never commit original game data or anything extracted from it, wherever it lands.
*.RFA
*.RFM
*.SDT
*.CAR
*.BIN

# Never commit a Ghidra project -- it's a disassembled/decompiled copy of the game binary.
*.gpr
*.rep/

# Godot. export_presets.cfg IS tracked: the "Open Fire" presets define the release (issue #61 stage 5) -- which
# files ship, and the openfire_import feature that points the game at the pack imported on the player's machine.
# Never put credentials in it (code signing passwords and the like go in the untracked .godot/export_credentials.cfg).
.godot/
.import/
export.cfg
*.translation
/export/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
/dist/
